# Amanah UI design

When adding or changing UI, follow `docs/design-guidelines.md`.

- Cream background, charcoal text, forest for focus/trust, sage for decoration only.
- Serif headings, sans-serif UI text. Arabic uses `font-arabic` with `lang="ar"` and `dir="rtl"`.
- Semantic color tokens; no raw hex in components; no new palette, gradients, or dark mode without approval.
- Phone first; `sm` (640px) is the main layout break. Narrow centered column (`max-w-3xl` content, `max-w-5xl` header).
- Visible focus rings (forest). Real buttons and links. Loading, empty, error, and success states on new screens.

If the guidelines list a conflict, ask before inventing a new default. Do not copy old screens or components.

Applied defaults for this codebase: report forms and primary form actions use 44px (`h-11`) controls with stronger field borders; keep the light-only palette.
